<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Home-screen sizes for the FOLLOWING widget, in the launcher's own grid units.

  Identical to the trending-posts widget's, and that is the point rather than a copy-paste: both
  widgets draw the SAME card (`FeedCardContent`), whose three designs are declared once in
  `FEED_CARD_SIZES`. A provider that offered a placement the card was not drawn for would land on
  a design it does not have.

  Every value is `70 × cells − 30` dp, the conversion the App Widget sizing guide gives for turning
  a cell count into the `minWidth` / `minHeight` a provider must declare
  (developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/appwidgets § "Determine widget sizing"):

      2 cells → 110dp    3 cells → 180dp    4 cells → 250dp    5 cells → 320dp

  They are separate resources rather than shared with the posts widget because a provider XML
  cannot be shared — each provider needs its own — and pointing two providers at one set of dimens
  would make retuning one silently retune the other.
-->
<resources>
  <!--
    Default placement: 4 cells wide by 3 tall — the design with the image slot, which is the one
    worth meeting the widget as.
  -->
  <dimen name="mention_following_widget_min_width">250dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="mention_following_widget_min_height">180dp</dimen>

  <!--
    The resize floor is 4 cells WIDE but only 2 tall. A post is a paragraph of text, and at 110dp
    across there is room for about three words per line, so letting it shrink that far would offer
    a size at which the card cannot do its job. Vertically it does shrink, to the design that drops
    the image and the rotation controls.
  -->
  <dimen name="mention_following_widget_min_resize_width">250dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="mention_following_widget_min_resize_height">110dp</dimen>

  <!--
    The ceiling is where the card runs out of content to reveal — five lines of text, a 120dp image,
    a byline and the control row — so a larger placement would only stretch what is there.
  -->
  <dimen name="mention_following_widget_max_resize_width">320dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="mention_following_widget_max_resize_height">320dp</dimen>
</resources>
